<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Turing returns eight weeks after his first visit, about eleven weeks after the last estrogen injection. The breast tenderness is less and he no longer notices it when running. Morning erections returned three weeks ago and his libido is coming back. He has had seven psychotherapy sessions and runs about 25 km a week. His mood is somewhat better, but he still feels flat most days, has little pleasure outside work, and wakes early. He has had no suicidal thoughts. After the last visit he asked to think about medicine; today, after a discussion of sertraline, mirtazapine, and bupropion and their effects on sexual function, weight, sleep, and blood pressure, he chose bupropion. He has no history of seizures, head injury, or an eating disorder and drinks little alcohol. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Breasts</td><td>Less tender; no discharge</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual function</td><td>Morning erections back for three weeks; libido returning</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Seven sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Running</td><td>About 25 km a week</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>12, down from 15</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

